  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation\n\n## Task Requirements\nCalculate the final position and velocity of a projectile launched at 45° with initial speed 30 m/s after 3 seconds.\n\n## Verification of Physics\nExpected values (using g = 9.81 m/s²):\n- v₀ₓ = 30·cos(45°) ≈ 21.2132 m/s; v₀ᵧ = 30·sin(45°) ≈ 21.2132 m/s\n- x = v₀ₓ·t = 21.2132 × 3 = **63.6396 m** ✓\n- y = v₀ᵧ·t − ½g·t² = 63.6396 − 44.145 = **19.4946 m** ✓\n- vₓ = **21.2132 m/s** (constant) ✓\n- vᵧ = v₀ᵧ − g·t = 21.2132 − 29.43 = **−8.2168 m/s** ✓\n\n## Screenshot Analysis\n1. **Screenshot 1**: Wolfram Alpha homepage with empty input box — starting state.\n2. **Screenshot 2**: Input box filled with the correct kinematic expressions: `30 cos(45 degrees)*3, 30 sin(45 degrees)*3 - 1/2*9.81*3^2, 30 cos(45 degrees), 30 sin(45 degrees) - 9.81*3` — these correctly encode x, y, vx, vy at t = 3 s.\n3. **Screenshots 3–5**: Results page confirms:\n   - Result pod: {45√2, 19.4946, 15√2, −8.2168} — matches the response's claim exactly.\n   - Decimal approximation pod: {63.6396, 19.4946, 21.2132, −8.2168} = (x, y, vx, vy) — matches the response exactly.\n\n## Response Consistency\n- The response's x, y, vx, vy values match the screenshot's decimal approximation pod perfectly.\n- Derived values not shown on the screenshot (distance from launch = 66.56 m and speed = 22.7490 m/s) are mathematically consistent: √(63.6396² + 19.4946²) ≈ 66.56 m and √(21.2132² + 8.2168²) ≈ 22.749 m/s. Per instructions, these unshown values are believable and correct.\n- Both required components (final position AND final velocity) are provided.\n\nThe computation was performed correctly on Wolfram Alpha with proper kinematic expressions, and all reported values are physically accurate.\n\n## Verdict\n**SUCCESS**",
